---
/* Component — PageHeader
 * The page's top bar. Its regions are PageHeaderStart, PageHeaderCenter and
 * PageHeaderEnd, placed by the consumer in that order. They carry daisyUI's own
 * navbar-start/-center/-end classes, rented as-is: their flex mechanics already
 * centre the middle child, so there is nothing to override there.
 *
 * Those mechanics depend on both halves being present — navbar-start and
 * navbar-end are each width:50%, while navbar-center has no width and does not
 * shrink. All three, or start plus end, behave as expected. A header carrying
 * *only* a centre is left-aligned rather than centred, and one carrying only an
 * end lands mid-bar rather than at the far edge, because its 50% box starts at
 * the inline edge and justifies within itself. Use start and end together to
 * keep the geometry predictable.
 *
 * The outer element keeps daisyUI's .navbar class, and this component's own
 * rule overrides it: display/align-items are redeclared explicitly (matching
 * daisyUI's values) so the box model here is fully self-contained rather than
 * leaning on daisyUI's layered rule, and min-height: 0 resets daisyUI's fixed
 * 4rem so block padding sizes the bar to its content.
 *
 * A full-width edge-to-edge band: as a direct child of Page (outside PageBody's
 * inline inset) it spans the whole window width on its own — no margins, no
 * bleed tricks — and the raised fill bleeds edge to edge with it. Flat and
 * cornerless, to read as chrome rather than a floating card. The inline padding
 * uses the same centred-column formula as PageBody: since padding insets the
 * *content* without shrinking the element's own box, the fill still spans full
 * width while the region content caps at --bravoixr-page-max and lines up with
 * the page column below. The fill themes with the page via the semantic dark
 * override. */
---

<header class="navbar">
  <slot />
</header>

<style>
  .navbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    min-height: 0;
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-inline: max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2));
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-raised);
  }
</style>
